        <nav class="breadcrumb reveal"><a href="index.html">Home</a> / <a href="kenya.html">Kenya</a> / Lamu &amp; the Coast</nav>
        <p class="article__lead reveal">Where the savanna ends, the Swahili coast begins — warm turquoise water, white sand, and the timeless island of Lamu, a place with no cars, only donkeys, dhows and centuries of culture. It's the perfect, soulful end to a Kenya safari.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Why visit Lamu &amp; the coast?</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Kenya's Indian-Ocean coast offers some of Africa's loveliest beaches and richest culture. Lamu, the jewel, blends Swahili, Arab and Indian heritage into something utterly its own — slow, gracious and deeply photogenic.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Lamu Old Town (UNESCO)</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Lamu Old Town is a UNESCO World Heritage Site — the oldest, best-preserved Swahili settlement in East Africa. Wander coral-stone alleys, carved doorways and bustling markets, with no traffic to break the spell.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Dhows &amp; the ocean</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Sailing a traditional wooden dhow at sunset is the quintessential Lamu experience. Add snorkelling, mangrove channels and fresh seafood feasts on the sand.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Barefoot beaches</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Shela's long, empty beach is the coast's most famous, but we can also set you on Diani's powder sand further south, or whisk you to a private island for total seclusion.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">The Lamu Yoga Festival</h2>
        <p class="reveal">Each year Lamu hosts the joyful <a href="lamu-yoga-festival.html">Lamu Yoga &amp; Wellbeing Festival</a> — five days of beachfront yoga, dhow cruises and Swahili feasts. It's one of our most-loved wellness trips.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Best time to visit</h2>
        <p class="reveal">The coast shines <strong>December–March</strong> (hot, sunny, calm seas) and again <strong>July–October</strong>. The long rains (April–May) are quieter. See our <a href="best-time-kenya.html">best time to visit Kenya</a> guide.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Where to stay &amp; how to get there</h2>
        <p class="reveal">We book beautiful Swahili houses and boutique hotels, all women-friendly. Lamu is a short flight from Nairobi or Mombasa, with a boat transfer to the islands — we handle every step.</p>

